    "collapsible_content_cGXRUN": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "tab_forme": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "I don't have PCOS and I'm not trying to get pregnant. Is this for me?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Yes. Inositol works on insulin signalling, and insulin resistance doesn't care about a diagnosis. It becomes more common in your forties and fifties as estrogen drops.</p><p>If you're tired after meals, reaching for something sweet mid-afternoon, gaining around your middle from foods that never used to matter, or waking at 3am, the mechanism applies whether or not it's written on a chart.</p><p>The 6-month study we quote on this page was in postmenopausal women. Not PCOS. Not fertility.*</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "tab_labs": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "My labs are normal. Why would insulin be the problem?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Because the standard panel measures glucose, not insulin.</p><p>Your body can hold glucose in range for years by producing more insulin to do the same job. Fasting glucose stays normal until much later. That compensation is the problem, and it's why so many women are told everything looks fine.</p><p>The tests that catch it: fasting insulin and HOMA-IR. Worth asking for by name.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "tab_when": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long before I notice anything?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>The afternoon crash and cravings usually shift first, often inside the first two weeks. Steadier energy tends to follow.</p><p>Insulin resistance itself takes longer. The postmenopausal trial measured its 75% drop at six months, on 4g a day, every day.* Stop at four weeks and you haven't given it a fair go. That's why the bundle is 90 days.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "tab_hrt": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I take it with HRT, metformin or a GLP-1?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Generally yes. Inositol isn't a hormone and it doesn't block anything. It's a compound your body already produces and uses, taken at a higher amount.</p><p>HRT works on estrogen. Metformin works mainly on glucose output from the liver. GLP-1s work on appetite and gastric emptying. Inositol works on insulin signalling inside the cell, a different part of the picture, which is why it's often used alongside them rather than instead of them.</p><p>If you're on prescription medication, run it past your doctor first.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "tab_powder": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why powder and not capsules?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>The studied dose is 4 grams a day. In capsule form, that's eight to ten capsules.</p><p>Powder is the only format where the full dose is realistic to take. Two scoops in your morning coffee and you're done.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "tab_taste": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What does it taste like? Does it actually dissolve?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Slightly sweet on its own. That's the inositol and the carob-sourced D-chiro, not added sweetener. There's nothing else in the tub to taste.</p><p>It dissolves clear, with no grit and no aftertaste, because there are no fillers or flow agents to leave residue. Coffee, water, a smoothie, whatever you already drink.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "tab_corn": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does this product contain corn?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p><strong>Our myo-inositol is derived from non-GMO corn.<br/><br/></strong>The myo-inositol is extracted from the corn, and the corn itself is left behind. If you have a corn sensitivity, we’d still recommend being mindful and checking with your doctor before you start.<br/><br/>Much of the corn grown today is genetically modified, so we only source from non-GMO corn. Corn is currently the most established source of myo-inositol, and we’ve chosen the highest-quality supply we could find.<br/><br/><strong>Our D-chiro-inositol is different. It comes from carob pods, where D-chiro occurs in higher amounts than anywhere else in nature.</strong> D-chiro does a lot of the heavy lifting on estrogen and androgen balance, so where it comes from matters.<br/><br/>Most brands make their D-chiro by converting myo-inositol from corn in a lab. We extract ours from carob instead. That keeps it as close to the source as possible. It’s also why our powder is naturally sweet and soft in texture, without any added flavor.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "tab_side": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Are there any side effects?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Inositol has a strong safety record. A small number of women notice some bloating or a change in digestion in the first few days, usually because 4g is a meaningful amount to introduce at once.</p><p>If that's you, start with one scoop and build to two over a week. It typically settles.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "tab_bundle": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What's in the 90-day bundle?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Two 6-week tubs, a 90-day supply at the full 2-scoop dose. $98 billed every 3 months as a subscription, which works out at $32.67 a month or $1.09 a day. It's our lowest price per day.</p><p>Every subscription comes with the free Metabolic Health Protocol (digital). You can skip or cancel anytime in your account.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "tab_refund": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What if it doesn't work for me?",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>You have 60 days. If it isn't doing anything for you, email us and we'll refund you. No phone call, no back-and-forth, no attempt to talk you out of it.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
